      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect. The answer is directly in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into that environment at all.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the API key by simply inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually use it to call the Anthropic API.",
